# realm-export-customers.template.json; env-specific redirect URIs, NEVER commit)
infra/keycloak/realm-export-customers.json

# Phase 18 verify-script output: last self-registered customer email (test artifact)
frontend/e2e/.last-customer-email
.qa-council/
docker-compose.frontend-3100.yml

# Phase 26 golden-render pre-change snapshots (k8s/scripts/render-golden.sh --snapshot):
# per-execution baselines for the --diff-since assertions in plans 26-01/26-02/26-04/26-08,
# never committed artifacts — keeping them untracked is what lets the `--write` idempotence
# check stay a clean `git diff --quiet k8s/goldens`.
k8s/goldens/.pre/

# Playwright screenshot output from e2e/media-review-320.spec.ts (evidence copies live in .planning)
e2e-artifacts/

# Phase 27 execution evidence (plan 27-02 and after). Carries tenant data and, during the
# broker migration, a full tar of the RabbitMQ data directory — a dead-letter export holds
# real webhook payloads and the volume snapshot holds every queued message. Never committed.
.evidence/

# Claude Code agent worktrees. Each is a FULL working copy of this repo, so a
# blanket `git add .` here stages tens of thousands of files belonging to another
# session's in-flight branches. Measured 2026-08-03: 9 live worktrees, 70,498
# untracked files. Ignore the worktree root ONLY — `.claude/skills/` is a
# supported location for tracked project skills and must stay visible.
.claude/worktrees/

# Scanner tool scratch (`.ua/` — config.json, fingerprints.json, intermediate/
# scan-result.json). Written into a module directory by tooling, not by the Go
# build, so `go clean` does not remove it and it reappears on every scan. Ignored
# rather than deleted: it is a cache, and the harm is only that it shows up
# untracked where a blanket `git add` would sweep 1.2 MB of tool state into a
# commit. Anchored to any depth because it lands beside whichever module ran.
.ua/

# Go coverage profile (edge-go). Generated by `go test -coverprofile=coverage.out ./...`
# and read by scripts/check-go-coverage.sh; CI uploads it as an artifact rather than
# committing it. Ignored so that running the gate locally does not leave an untracked
# ~20KB build artefact for a blanket `git add` to sweep into a commit.
edge-go/coverage.out
